{"timestamp":1774802781787,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"36a8cafc-a247-4eaa-a416-25fc25b0b719","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01F2ed38urpvxBruWe6zUj5s","payload":{"session_id":"36a8cafc-a247-4eaa-a416-25fc25b0b719","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-experience-apps-mas-trees-032a79ab/36a8cafc-a247-4eaa-a416-25fc25b0b719.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/032a79ab","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/032a79ab/.pinata/specs/issue-032a79ab-adw-6-sdlc_planner-geo-tiered-cta-mode-toggle.md","content":"# Plan: Geo-tiered CTA mode toggle\n\n## Summary\nAdd a `ctaMode` settings flag (`default` | `buy-only` | `trial-only`) that can be set per geo/locale in Studio and delivered via MAS-IO settings. When the flag is active, `hydrate.js` suppresses the non-active CTA type at render time before the card is attached to the DOM \u2014 no card fragment content is modified.\n\n## Task Description\nImplement a settings-based CTA mode toggle across three domains: (1) register `ctaMode` as a known setting in MAS-IO so it is included in the settings payload, (2) add swap logic in `hydrate.js` that reads `settings.ctaMode` and suppresses the conflicting CTA type from the rendered card, including a Learn More fallback for unpaired single-CTA placements, and (3) add `ctaMode` to the Studio settings name map so admin can author and preview the flag.\n\n## Relevant Files\n\n| File | Action | Why |\n|------|--------|-----|\n| `io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.js` | Edit | Add `ctaMode` to `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS` so it is recognised and delivered via the settings pipeline |\n| `web-components/src/hydrate.js` | Edit | Add `processCtaMode()` function and call it from `hydrate()` after `processCTAs()` |\n| `studio/src/settings/setting-name-map.js` | Edit | Re-exports `SETTING_NAME_BY_VALUE`; the new entry in `settings.js` is auto-included, but verify `getSettingDefaultValue` handles `select` editor type |\n| `web-components/test/hydrate.test.js` | Edit | Add unit tests for `processCtaMode` |\n| `io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.test.js` | Edit | Add test asserting `ctaMode` is extracted and propagated as a text setting |\n\n## Step by Step Tasks\n\n### 1. Register `ctaMode` in SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS\n- In `io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.js`, add to `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS`:\n  ```js\n  { name: 'ctaMode', valueType: 'text', editor: 'select' },\n  ```\n- This makes `extractValue` return the `textValue` (`default`, `buy-only`, or `trial-only`) and `applySettings` writes it to `fragment.settings.ctaMode`\n- No other changes needed in the IO pipeline \u2014 locale-override resolution already works for `text` type\n\n### 2. Add `getSettingDefaultValue` support for `select` editor\n- In `studio/src/settings/setting-name-map.js`, add a branch in `getSettingDefaultValue`:\n  ```js\n  if (definition.editor === 'select') return 'default';\n  ```\n- This prevents the Studio UI from rendering an undefined default for the new select-type setting\n\n### 3. Implement `processCtaMode` in hydrate.js\n\n**CTA type detection** \u2014 a CTA element is a trial CTA if it has `data-modal=\"twp\"` on itself or on its inner `checkout-button`/`checkout-link`; otherwise it is a buy CTA.\n\nAdd to `web-components/src/hydrate.js`:\n```js\nexport function processCtaMode(fields, merchCard, settings) {\n    const ctaMode = settings?.ctaMode;\n    if (!ctaMode || ctaMode === 'default') return;\n\n    const footer = merchCard.querySelector('[slot]'); // CTA footer slot\n    if (!footer) return;\n    const allCtas = [...footer.querySelectorAll('a, checkout-button, checkout-link, sp-button')];\n    if (!allCtas.length) return;\n\n    const isTrialCta = (el) =>\n        el.dataset?.modal === 'twp' ||\n        el.getAttribute('data-modal') === 'twp';\n\n    const suppressMode = ctaMode === 'buy-only' ? 'trial' : 'buy'; // which type to remove\n\n    const toSuppress = allCtas.filter((el) =>\n        suppressMode === 'trial' ? isTrialCta(el) : !isTrialCta(el),\n    );\n    const toKeep = allCtas.filter((el) =>\n        suppressMode === 'trial' ? !isTrialCta(el) : isTrialCta(el),\n    );\n\n    if (toKeep.length > 0) {\n        // Fully remove suppressed CTAs from DOM\n        toSuppress.forEach((el) => el.remove());\n    } else {\n        // All CTAs are the suppressed type \u2014 replace with Learn More fallback\n        const learnMoreUrl = fields?.learnMoreUrl || '#';\n        const learnMoreLabel = fields?.learnMoreLabel || 'Learn More';\n        const fallback = createTag('a', { href: learnMoreUrl, class: 'learn-more-fallback' }, learnMoreLabel);\n        footer.innerHTML = '';\n        footer.append(fallback);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Wire `processCtaMode` into `hydrate()`\n- In the `hydrate()` function in `hydrate.js`, after the `processCTAs(...)` call, add:\n  ```js\n  processCtaMode(fields, merchCard, settings);\n  ```\n- `settings` is already destructured from `fragment` at the top of `hydrate()`\n\n### 5. Add unit tests for `processCtaMode`\n- In `web-components/test/hydrate.test.js`:\n  - `buy-only` with dual CTAs: only trial CTA removed, buy CTA retained\n  - `trial-only` with dual CTAs: only buy CTA removed, trial CTA retained\n  - `buy-only` with single trial-only CTA: replaced by Learn More link\n  - `trial-only` with single buy-only CTA: replaced by Learn More link\n  - `default` mode: no changes applied\n  - No CTAs present: no error thrown\n\n### 6. Add test for settings pipeline\n- In `io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.test.js` (or equivalent test file):\n  - Assert that a settings fragment with `name: 'ctaMode'` and `textValue: 'buy-only'` results in `fragment.settings.ctaMode === 'buy-only'`\n  - Assert locale override for ctaMode resolves correctly for a matching locale\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- `fragment.settings.ctaMode` is populated when a `ctaMode` settings entry exists in AEM for the current locale\n- When `ctaMode=buy-only`, all elements with `data-modal=\"twp\"` in the CTA footer are removed from the DOM before the card is shown\n- When `ctaMode=trial-only`, all non-trial CTA elements in the footer are removed from the DOM\n- When only the suppressed CTA type is present and `learnMoreUrl` is set in fields, a plain anchor fallback is rendered in place\n- When `ctaMode=default` or is absent, no CTA changes are made\n- No empty `[slot]` containers are left after swap (CTAs removed, not hidden)\n- `node --check` passes on all modified JS files\n\n## Validation Commands\n- `node --check web-components/src/hydrate.js`\n- `node --check io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.js`\n- `node --check studio/src/settings/setting-name-map.js`\n- Run existing test suite: `npm test --workspace=web-components` (or equivalent per repo)\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F2ed38urpvxBruWe6zUj5s"}}
